Each letter represents a non-zero digit. What is the value of $t?$ \begin{align*}
c + o &= u \\
u + n &= t \\
t + c &= s \\
o + n + s &= 12
\end{align*}

solution_steps:
We can write \[\frac{1}{n^2 + n} = \frac{1}{n(n+1)} = \frac{(n+1) - n}{n(n+1)} = \frac{1}{n} - \frac{1}{n+1}.\]
Thus, our sum telescopes: \[\sum_{n=1}^{1000} \frac{1}{n^2 + n} = \left(\frac{1}{1} - \frac{1}{2}\right) + \left(\frac{1}{2} - \frac{1}{3}\right) + \dots + \left(\frac{1}{999} - \frac{1}{1000}\right) + \left(\frac{1}{1000} - \frac{1}{1001}\right) = \frac{1}{1} - \frac{1}{1001} = \boxed{\frac{1000}{1001}}.\]
The answer is: \frac{1000}{1001}

