solution_steps:
First, we perform the multiplication and division from left to right:
\begin{align*}
-\left(14\div 2\cdot 9-60+3\cdot 9\right) &= -\left(7\cdot 9-60+3\cdot 9\right) \\
&= -\left(63-60+3\cdot 9\right) \\
&= -\left(63-60+27\right).
\end{align*}
Next, we perform the addition and subtraction from left to right:
\begin{align*}
-\left(63-60+27\right) &= -\left(3+27\right) \\
&= -30.
\end{align*}
Therefore, the value of the expression is $\boxed{-30}$.The answer is: -30

