We can find the residue of $9^{2010}$ modulo 17 by repeatedly squaring 9 and taking the remainder after each step.
\begin{align*}
9^2 &\equiv 81 \equiv 13 \pmod{17} \\
9^4 &\equiv 13^2 \equiv 169 \equiv 16 \pmod{17} \\
9^8 &\equiv 16^2 \equiv 256 \equiv 1 \pmod{17}
\end{align*}
Since $9^8 \equiv 1 \pmod{17}$, we can write $9^{2010}$ as $(9^8)^{251} \cdot 9^2 \equiv 1^{251} \cdot 13 \equiv \boxed{13} \pmod{17}$.
The answer is: 13

