In this case, we have $\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w} = (-10)(15) + (6)(-9) = -150 - 54 = -204$ and $\|\mathbf{w}\|^2 = (15)^2 + (-9)^2 = 225 + 81 = 306$.
Therefore, the projection of $\mathbf{v}$ onto $\mathbf{w}$ is \[ \text{proj}_\mathbf{w} \mathbf{v} = \frac{-204}{306} \begin{pmatrix} 15 \\ -9 \end{pmatrix} = \frac{-2}{3} \begin{pmatrix} 15 \\ -9 \end{pmatrix} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}}. \] The answer is: \begin{pmatrix}-10\6\end{pmatrix}

